{
  "case_id": "2016-15-118",
  "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nROBERT C. HILLIARD, ESQ., Corpus Christi, Tex.; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nRANDOLPH J. ORTEGA, ESQ., El Paso, Tex.; on behalf of the Respondent Mesa.\nEDWIN S. KNEEDLER, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Federal Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Robert C. HILLIARD (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HILLIARD: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\n15-year-old Sergio Hernandez was standing in Mexico, barely across the border, unthreatening and unarmed, when he was shot and killed by a U.S. Border Patrol agent standing inside the United States.\nThis tragic case is one of the most simplest extraterritorial cases this Court will ever have in front of it for five reasons.\nFirst, all of the conduct of the domestic police officer happened inside the United States.\nSecond, it was a civilian domestic police officer.\nThird it was a civilian plaintiff, not an enemy combatant. Fourth, it was one of the most fundamental rights, the right to life. Fifth, the other government involved supports -- the government of Mexico supports the claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So is that -- I was trying to figure out from your brief what exactly your rule is.\nSo are all five of those necessary, in your view, for there to be a Bivens claim? Is anything else necessary?\nIs that exactly the rule that you want us to adopt?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: We know that part. The question is: what words do we write so that this opinion doesn't affect the drone strike, which is what you seem to want?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: So the rule would apply there.\nMR. HILLIARD: The rule would apply if he was 19, standing unarmed in Mexico, when he was shot.\nJUSTICE ALITO: All right. What if he was armed, but he had his hands up?\nMR. HILLIARD: Again, we're not asking for a win here. We're simply asking if the Constitution applies and that he can -- he can -- the defense of self-defense by the officer can happen at the trial court then."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Right. So suppose he violates that rule. He -- he --\nMR. HILLIARD: Well --\nJUSTICE ALITO: -- crosses into Mexico and then he shoots the --\nMR. HILLIARD: Right.\nJUSTICE ALITO: -- the Mexican nationals.\nMR. HILLIARD: Right. It may not -- the rule would not apply, but it doesn't mean that under Boumediene standards that there's not constitutional protections. Did he not know where the line was? Did he intentionally go in hot pursuit? Was he called over by a federale? The specifics of the facts would affect the decision of whether the Constitution applied.\nUnder our -- under our proposed rule, as Mexico pointed out in its brief, there's been 243 shootings along the border with the Border Patrol using deadly force, 10 of those across the border."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it -- is your rule that if the U.S. agent commits on foreign soil an action that would be a violation had it occurred within the United States, there is a Bivens claim and there is a Fourth Amendment violation? Is that your rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do -- an anterior question. It has been argued that the Constitution is only for people who are within the United States; therefore, an alien injured abroad has no Fourth or Fifth Amendment rights. How do you answer that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, but the one obvious difference with Boumediene is in there, you were dealing with an area subject to an exclusive control of the United States. Here, you're dealing with Mexico, an entirely different situation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "injury occurs in a different jurisdiction; right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, my -- I -- I -- I've waited while the rule was being discussed because that's important; but as Justice Kagan's question indicates, whether or not there can and should be a Bivens action is critical to your case.\nSince 1988, this Court has not recognized a single Bivens action. We look for special considerations. You've indicated that there's a problem all along the border. Why doesn't that counsel us that this is one of the most sensitive areas of foreign affairs where the political branches should discuss with Mexico what the solution ought to be?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hilliard",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you start with -- you start in your opinion that the -- that if all of the conduct happens inside the United States and -- and there's a close proximity cross-border shooting, then the Fourth Amendment -- Fourth Amendment constraints on deadly force apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: So, Mr. Hilliard, you want me to put down in my notes the location of the boy is irrelevant to this case. That's what -- that's what we're going to put in our opinion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hilliard",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HILLIARD: So the curtilage cases were used in order to show that there is a -- a substantive reasonableness evaluation in -- in regards to the close proximity requirement of our rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Ortega",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Fourth Amendment does not apply in a cross-border shooting of a Mexican civilian on Mexico soil by a United States Federal agent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Could I ask you briefly, because we haven't talked about it yet, a question on the qualified immunity point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Would you recognize that -- let's say it was the -- the boy that the Border Patrol grabbed and then shot him, so the -- the -- so the death would have occurred in the United States, Bivens claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: So does it make a whole lot of sense to say if the officer shoots somebody on the U.S. side of the border, good Bivens claim? If the officer standing in the same place shoots somebody who's just across the border, no claim? That doesn't make a whole lot of sense, does it, to distinguish those two victims?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: So you wanted to talk about the Fourth Amendment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-118",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a0133059bf61-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    },
    {
